From: Gaussian Scene Restoration Project
Date: 2026-07-05
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] model_wrapper: Add gaussian_scene_restorer to optimizer
 high-lr group

When the restorer is enabled and the encoder is frozen, the restorer's parameters
need a higher learning rate than the (zero-update) backbone. This patch adds
"gaussian_scene_restorer" to the name-based grouping in configure_optimizers()
so restorer parameters get the main learning rate while backbone parameters
get backbone_lr_multiplier * lr (typically 0.0).

---
 src/model/model_wrapper.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/model/model_wrapper.py b/src/model/model_wrapper.py
index e969e38f..3ebd8402 100644
--- a/src/model/model_wrapper.py
+++ b/src/model/model_wrapper.py
@@ -808,7 +808,7 @@ class ModelWrapper(LightningModule):
             if not param.requires_grad:
                 continue

-            if "gaussian_param_head" in name or "interm" in name:
+            if "gaussian_param_head" in name or "interm" in name or "gaussian_scene_restorer" in name:
                 new_params.append(param)
                 new_param_names.append(name)
             else:
